color="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-009: Paragraph | P2 --><section id="1009" layout-row="true"><div layout-row="true"><table layout-row="true" role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr layout-row="true"> <td valign="top" align="left"> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="wrap"> <tbody><tr> <td align="left" style="padding: 0px 20px 16px 20px" class="pad20rl match"><p style="font-size: 14px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 150%; margin: 0px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: 0px; text-transform: none; color: #333333; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" enable-personalization="true" data-richtext="p2_text" data-groupid="p2" class="mobile_p1"><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 150%;">Can organizations do more to plan their responses to external shocks?<br><br>Geopolitical uncertainty is no longer something leaders can monitor from the sidelines. Today, geopolitical considerations are becoming more central to strategy, and <span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/capabilities/geopolitics/our-insights/the-art-science-and-technology-of-geopolitical-scenario-planning?__hScId__=v710000019ec6b26353a932606e966eb1e0&__hRlId__=0a481dfa6d1846510000021ef3a0bcd1&__hDId__=0a481dfa-6d18-4651-8e8b-50aa0376cff2&__hSD__=d3d3Lm1ja2luc2V5LmNvbQ==&cid=mgp_opr-eml-alt-pub-mgp-glb--bundle&hlkid=4ae1e45abd2648bfaaf268e09c75e2da&hctky=17208988&hdpid=0a481dfa-6d18-4651-8e8b-50aa0376cff2" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="87f92410651011f1b4f65f06b79ae577">scenario planning</a></span> can help leaders move from reacting to events to proactively shaping their response.<br><br>“Identifying an objective, choosing the right foresight method to achieve it, and building the capabilities to spot risks and opportunities requires the recognition that there is no crystal ball—only disciplined preparation,” write <span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/T/v710000019ec6b26353a932606e966eb1e0/0a481dfa6d1846510000021ef3a0bcd2/0a481dfa-6d18-4651-8e8b-50aa0376cff2?__dU__=v0G4RBKTXg2GsTlMa8YbE0npiPHb7Gzq29ujr-mrJsl6bcn0E30HNSquNCCrd1XNAz&__F__=v0fUYvjHMDjRPMSh3tviDHXIoXcPxvDgUUCCPvXMWoX_0JoZLAZABQFzGdi2cn1iU7KJEa5whIrwYtzM-cxLg6GesZ5R5dH2Df0cMJ1S6PQfROwBj3J-3fRdQHGyO2N79Hm_19x_vCYiFJUe6SXKHtS8CZMzC2yHhtwu2E8R08afaMXqpWUVWJWUQGhcZQbGUwCPgYrNb8FBZmFOPMa1Fif9vPfDo5cdJMSq1Xnud7lie6DJV1nH3oY4BlZkX4fO0GTJ3pwktL1uDswM_PlnW8wqTDTLyxF_HTuVsyW7KaXMfnzAdkln2Ur1rey7xcz36kTgOvL5p7KqGRTz3u1C43Yq6d3barlwlRIWlL1R_FdJYCTG5dmwz0ClE6gUMGGtRRmvo7d6ZXJIjGSKLVVS4pzt7CBAJvB6XTIwOvZNBUrJY5EMtGo2mj1TIDcvazpTbuasaUlaZ7IAcrtfTUxVpGjbyJ4k10kNp2imVCVmadFqc8Aa7aSnJ5J5hZPJArccXegSZ3IWs8QGs=" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="98f4faf0651011f1b4f65f06b79ae577">Ziad Haider</a></span>, <span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/T/v710000019ec6b26353a932606e966eb1e0/0a481dfa6d1846510000021ef3a0bcd3/0a481dfa-6d18-4651-8e8b-50aa0376cff2?__dU__=v0G4RBKTXg2GsTlMa8YbE0npiPHb7Gzq29ujr-mrJsl6bcn0E30HNSquNCCrd1XNAz&__F__=v0fUYvjHMDjRPMSh3tviDHXIoXcPxvDgUUCCPvXMWoX_0JoZLAZABQFzGdi2cn1iU7KJEa5whIrwYtzM-cxLg6GaZmKeAEULNG8BZScQuSy0GDS6GkpyCwdOn06UX9mQ9cGPO7MKWD0EapA3gM19s0q2fDRer4YVzolFpE-jcjorZyiLu1sgn-fDZ-VpAG8jhDNSQGUlDjIsKZIY7riRSTgEYZvq8d_2vTWHHluoFkO9-Lh98rEr9AV2zk_GQu547mlSFb26jRbzPTO7mjwJq8XYUFNZ6vGyNSBW3Ps6QwqrrBWpVCyY6NEAj9_OitRY6HCJ7FoG6bz27byQThZdbIJ3EDDsPUQZR9QsKiY9Iar5Fp--0NmiIXQHOeaMRioRSuLgUuS1lmE6NZTb4OFTYkNF4kNu9YcGMaMtnnJw51EqaBRV7qQGyE0n_YJAKlUa9YGpCzPlo0-vtvP6CM5LUqCLmvoUyWbsrve-cpJheNUG3dYjXFUDpsR0c1w5kEu